    "result_text": "Only one test class exists and the build is green. Done.\n\nI implemented the postcode-preferred locality derivation:\n\n- **`Region.java`** \u2014 added `forPostcode(String)`, which parses the postcode and returns the region whose inclusive range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) contains it, or `null` when absent, non-numeric, or out of range. It reuses the existing `acceptsPostcode` predicate.\n- **`LocalityResolver.java`** \u2014 `deriveLocality` now takes `(city, postcode)`, looks up the region by postcode first and only falls back to `Region.forCity` when the postcode yields nothing, still returning `UNKNOWN` when neither matches.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping expression now passes `owner.getPostcode()` alongside `owner.getCity()`.\n\nKnown cities still resolve to the same region (their postcodes and city table agree), while cities sharing a name are now disambiguated by postcode. `./mvnw test` passes: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
