    "probe_text": "Serving endpoint: `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:163`). Here is everything applied, in execution order. **[V]** marks a validation (can reject the request), **[S]** marks a side-effect (mutates the payload, the new owner, other rows, or logs).\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN`.\n2. **[V] Bean Validation** on the `@Valid @RequestBody` payload (`OwnerFieldsDto` / `Owner`), all of which run before any controller code:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (letters with up to two space/apostrophe/hyphen-separated parts).\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`).\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`.\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`.\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`.\n   - `email` (optional) \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`.\n   - `postcode` (optional) \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`.\n3. **[S]** A transaction is opened (`@Transactional`), so any later rejection rolls back the household back-fill writes from step 12.\n\n## Inside `normalizeAndValidate` (`:199`)\n\n4. **[S] Address normalization** \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.normalize` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`); the canonical value is written back onto the payload.\n5. **[V] Required-fields check** (`validateRequiredFields`, `:310`) \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank; because it runs after step 4, an address that is blank once normalized is rejected \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n6. **[V] Postcode region check** (`validatePostcode`, `:338`) \u2014 only if a postcode was supplied: if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) the postcode must fall in that region's range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n7. **[S/V] Telephone normalization** \u2014 `TelephoneNormalizer.normalize` converts to E.164 (assumes `+61`, drops a leading `0`, strips non-digits); the result is written back. This also **[V]** rejects a number that isn't 8\u201315 digits, or whose national-number length is wrong for a known country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n8. **[V] City capacity** (`requireCityHasCapacity`, `:376`) \u2014 reject if the city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `OwnerCityFullException`.\n9. **[S] Registration-date resolution** (`resolveRegistrationDate`, `:221`) \u2014 default to the server's current date when omitted, then roll a Saturday/Sunday forward to Monday; the adjusted date is written back onto the payload.\n10. **[V] Daily limit** (`requireDailyLimitNotReached`, `:240`) \u2014 reject if \u2265 100 existing owners already carry that adjusted registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n11. **[S] Email normalization** \u2014 `EmailNormalizer.normalize` lower-cases a present email (blank/null left untouched); written back onto the payload.\n\n## Back in `addOwner` (`:166` onward)\n\n12. **[S]** Map the payload to a new `Owner` (`ownerMapper.toOwner`; `id` and `pets` ignored).\n13. **[S] `customerCode`** set (`generateCustomerCode`, `:276`) \u2014 `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where `NNNN` is a per-city sequence = (owners already in that city) + 1.\n14. **[S] `namesakeCount`** set (`countNamesakes`, `:293`) \u2014 number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n15. **[S] `bulkSignupWarning`** set (`computeBulkSignupWarning`, `:259`) \u2014 `true` when > 80 owners already carry that registration date.\n16. **[S] Household assignment** (`assignHouseholdId`, `:416`) \u2014 only if `sharesHousehold == true` **and** existing owners match the same last name + normalized address: derive a stable `householdId` (SHA-256 based) onto the new owner, and **back-fill and persist** that `householdId` onto any matching existing members that lacked it (a write to other rows).\n17. **[V] Duplicate/identity check** (`requireUniqueIdentity`, `:360`) \u2014 reject if any existing owner has the same derived `identityKey` (`<canonical telephone>|<email>|<householdId>`) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException`. Runs after step 16 so the key reflects the assigned household.\n18. **[S] Persist** the new owner (`clinicService.saveOwner`), assigning its `id`.\n19. **[S] Audit log** \u2014 one line to the `AUDIT` logger with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membership level.\n20. **[S] `householdMemberCount`** populated (`populateHouseholdMemberCount`, `:454`) \u2014 transient count of owners sharing the `householdId` (1 when none).\n21. **[S] Response mapping** \u2014 `toOwnerDto` stamps derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`).\n22. **[S]** `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header set; return `201 Created`.\n\nNote ordering nuances worth calling out: required-field and postcode validation happen *after* address normalization; the city-capacity, daily-limit, and namesake/customer-code counts all read the current owner list *before* the new owner is saved (so none count the owner being created); and the household back-fill in step 16 writes to other owner rows even though it's part of creating this one."
